2026-06-19 16:03:34,097 | INFO | HTTP Request: POST http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/chat "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
2026-06-19 16:03:34,097 | AGENT | AIInnovation Agent answered: To address the client's requirements for an AI assistance solution that supports hospital staff in their daily activities, facilitates access to information, improves the quality of written outputs, and reduces processing and documentation times, I propose leveraging our company's existing capabilities in retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) and hybrid retrieval.

Our RAG approach can be applied to develop a solution that provides intelligent assistance to hospital staff by generating answers grounded in the organization's own validated documents, such as care protocols, internal procedures, and regulatory texts. This will enable staff to quickly access reliable and up-to-date information, reducing the time spent searching for relevant information.

To improve the quality of written outputs, our template-guided drafting capability can be utilized to assist staff in generating high-quality clinical and administrative content, such as discharge summaries, medical reports, and patient letters. This will help reduce the time spent on documentation tasks and ensure that outputs meet expected quality standards.

Our solution will also incorporate explainability and traceability features, providing source citations, retrieved passages, and a retrieval trace for every interaction. This will enable hospital staff to understand the basis for recommendations or suggestions made by the AI system, ensuring transparency and trust in the decision-making process.

In terms of innovation strategy, we will adopt an iterative approach, working closely with the client's experts to select and curate a relevant corpus of documents, tune the retrieval model, design prompts and templates per use case, and evaluate the solution through a labelled evaluation set. This collaborative approach will ensure that the solution meets the specific needs of the hospital staff and is aligned with the organization's goals and objectives.

Furthermore, our commitment to data sovereignty and security will be ensured by hosting the solution on infrastructure that complies with relevant regulatory requirements, such as the French Hébergeur de Données de Santé (HDS) certification. This will guarantee the protection of sensitive health data and ensure that the solution is designed with privacy and security in mind.

By leveraging our existing capabilities in RAG, hybrid retrieval, and template-guided drafting, and adopting an iterative innovation strategy, we can develop a comprehensive AI assistance solution that addresses the client's requirements while ensuring explainability, traceability, and compliance with regulatory requirements.
